  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n{他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\nPattern: Xを{拵|こしら}える\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{拵|こしら}えている indicates ongoing action (in the process of making).\n\nREGISTER:\nSlightly literary or old-fashioned. More commonly used in written language or by older speakers. {作|つく}る is the neutral everyday equivalent.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {料理|りょうり}を{拵|こしら}える - to prepare a meal\n- {言|い}い{訳|わけ}を{拵|こしら}える - to make up an excuse\n- {話|はなし}を{拵|こしら}える - to fabricate a story\n\nUSAGE:\nCompared to {作|つく}る, {拵|こしら}える suggests more care, craftsmanship, or a traditional approach. Often used for food preparation and handmade items.",
